<title>UK: Bulker sails from Ulsan after tanker collision.</title>
<headline>Bulker sails from Ulsan after tanker collision.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maltese-flag tanker Tomis Providence moved to an outer anchorage, Ulsan, South Korea, after completing discharge of its cargo, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The 88,850-dwt tanker which had been involved in a collision with the Chinese-flag bulker Bao Shan Hai at Ulsan on July 22, was now awaiting its owners' decision.</p>
<p>The 64,910-dwt bulker sailed from Ulsan on July 29 bound for Xingang after completion of cargo discharge.</p>
<p>Temporary repairs to the bulker were made during cargo discharge, with permanent repairs to be carried out in China.</p>
</text>
